1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Section 2

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,003
Good evening everyone.

3
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:04,931
My name's Phil Sutton,

4
00:00:04,931 --> 00:00:08,061
and I'm chairman of the Highways Committee.

5
00:00:08,061 --> 00:00:15,217
We've called this meeting to inform members of the public about the new regulations for traffic

6
00:00:15,217 --> 00:00:17,900
and parking we're proposing for Granford.

7
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:24,600
I'll start by summarising these changes before we open the meeting to questions.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,096
So, why do we need to make these changes to traffic systems in Granford?

9
00:00:31,096 --> 00:00:36,200
Well, we're very aware that traffic is becoming an increasing problem.

10
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,965
It's been especially noticeable with the increase in heavy traffic while they've been building

11
00:00:41,965 --> 00:00:43,200
the new hospital.

12
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:48,800
But it's the overall rise in the volume of traffic of all kinds that's

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:49,600
concerning us.

14
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,600
To date there's not been any increase in traffic accidents,

15
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,600
but that's not something we want to see happen, obviously.

16
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:02,229
We recently carried out a survey of local residents,

17
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,800
and their responses were interesting.

18
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:10,209
People were very concerned about the lack of visibility on some roads due to

19
00:01:10,209 --> 00:01:13,300
cars parked along the sides of the roads.

20
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:19,482
We'd expected complaints about the congestion near the school when parents are dropping off their children

21
00:01:19,482 --> 00:01:21,027
or picking them up,

22
00:01:21,027 --> 00:01:23,732
but this wasn't top of the list,

23
00:01:23,732 --> 00:01:29,141
and nor were noise and fumes from trucks and lorries, though they were mentioned

24
00:01:29,141 --> 00:01:30,300
by some people.

25
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,986
We think these new traffic regulations would make a lot of difference.

26
00:01:34,986 --> 00:01:38,500
But we still have a long way to go.

27
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,730
We've managed to keep our proposals within budget, just,

28
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:44,602
so they can be covered by the Council.

29
00:01:44,602 --> 00:01:49,627
But, of course, it's no good introducing new regulations if we don't have a

30
00:01:49,627 --> 00:01:52,498
way of making sure that everyone obeys them,

31
00:01:52,498 --> 00:01:57,523
and that's an area we're still working on with the help of representatives from

32
00:01:57,523 --> 00:01:58,600
the police force.

33
00:01:58,600 --> 00:01:59,031
OK,

34
00:01:59,031 --> 00:02:07,215
so this slide shows a map of the central area of Granford, with the High Street in the middle

35
00:02:07,215 --> 00:02:09,800
and School Road on the right.

36
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:14,747
Now, we already have a set of traffic lights in the High Street at

37
00:02:14,747 --> 00:02:16,513
the junction with Station Road,

38
00:02:16,513 --> 00:02:21,460
but we're planning to have another set at the other end, at the School

39
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:25,700
Road junction, to regulate the flow of traffic along the High Street.

40
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:30,700
We've decided we definitely need a pedestrian crossing.

41
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:34,675
We considered putting this on School Road, just outside the school,

42
00:02:34,675 --> 00:02:40,095
but in the end we decided that could lead to a lot of traffic congestion

43
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:45,155
so we decided to locate it on the High Street, crossing the road in

44
00:02:45,155 --> 00:02:46,600
front of the supermarket.

45
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,282
That's a very busy area,

46
00:02:48,282 --> 00:02:50,300
so it should help things there.

47
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,846
We're proposing some changes to parking.

48
00:02:52,846 --> 00:02:57,939
At present, parking isn't allowed on the High Street outside the library,

49
00:02:57,939 --> 00:03:00,485
but we're going to change that,

50
00:03:00,485 --> 00:03:02,183
and allow parking there,

51
00:03:02,183 --> 00:03:07,700
but not at the other end of the High Street near School Road.

52
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:13,402
There'll be a new 'No Parking' sign on School Road, just by the entrance

53
00:03:13,402 --> 00:03:16,661
to the school, forbidding parking for 25 metres.

54
00:03:16,661 --> 00:03:22,363
This should improve visibility for drivers and pedestrians, especially on the bend just to

55
00:03:22,363 --> 00:03:24,400
the north of the school.

56
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:30,719
As far as disabled drivers are concerned, at present they have parking outside the

57
00:03:30,719 --> 00:03:31,170
supermarket,

58
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:33,878
but lorries also use those spaces,

59
00:03:33,878 --> 00:03:40,197
so we've got two new disabled parking spaces on the side road up towards

60
00:03:40,197 --> 00:03:41,100
the bank.

61
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,510
It's not ideal,

62
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:45,800
but probably better than the present arrangement.

63
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:50,500
We also plan to widen the pavement on School Road.

64
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:54,337
We think we can manage to get an extra half-metre on the bend just

65
00:03:54,337 --> 00:03:57,900
before you get to the school, on the same side of the road.

66
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:03,550
Finally, we've introduced new restrictions on loading and unloading for the supermarket,

67
00:04:03,550 --> 00:04:09,200
so lorries will only be allowed to stop there before 8 am.

68
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:15,394
That's the supermarket on School Road - we kept to the existing arrangements with

69
00:04:15,394 --> 00:04:17,300
the High Street supermarket.

70
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,138
OK.

71
00:04:18,138 --> 00:04:21,488
So that's about it.

72
00:04:21,488 --> 00:04:24,000
Now, would anyone ...
